  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 135 AM CDT Wed Sep 23 2026\n\nThe upper high will remain near the TX coast through the end of the \nweek. Strong subsidence from this feature will bring an end to the \nafternoon convection we've been seeing. The airmass over South-\nCentral Texas remain about the same with low level flow from the \neast to southeast. Temperatures will will also be stagnant through \nthe weekend. It will feel like an endless summer rather than the \nstart of fall. For the start of next week, the upper high will slide \nto the south. The height falls associated with this movement may \nallow convection to develop along the northern edge of the high \nacross our northern counties Monday and Tuesday afternoons. Chances \nwill be better Tuesday as the high moves farther away.",
